    {
      "idx": 9,
      "question": "I need help reviewing yesterday’s application activity logs.  \n    First, find yesterday’s log file somewhere under my MCP directory (it should have “yesterday” in the filename), then read its contents so we can understand what’s inside.  \n    After that, please set up a structured plan of tasks for analyzing the log, summarizing key events, and preparing a short report for me.",
      "servers": {
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem": [
          "search_files",
          "read_text_file"
        ],
        "@kazuph/mcp-taskmanager": [
          "request_planning"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "idx": 24,
      "question": "I want to turn yesterday’s log entries into actionable tasks. Please read the file at txt/log_yesterday.txt, analyze the problems mentioned in it, and then add a set of “To Do” items into a new task file named logs_tasks.md based on what needs follow‑up.",
      "servers": {
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem": [
          "read_text_file"
        ],
        "server-sequential-thinking": [
          "sequentialthinking"
        ],
        "mcp-tasks": [
          "tasks_setup",
          "tasks_add"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "idx": 117,
      "question": "I am planning to develop an AI-driven application that analyzes real-time transportation data to optimize travel routes. Please create and analyze the tasks required to implement this feature. Then, break them into manageable subtasks tied to completion criteria. Additionally, think through the sequential process needed to verify the efficiency and real-time capability of the solutions for refining tasks further. Finally, search for similar past tasks in our archives that may provide reusable insights or components.",
      "servers": {
        "mcp-shrimp-task-manager": [
          "plan_task",
          "analyze_task",
          "split_tasks"
        ],
        "mcp-tasks": [
          "tasks_setup",
          "tasks_search"
        ],
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking": [
          "sequentialthinking"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "idx": 416,
      "question": "I need to implement a new log analysis feature for our application. The system should parse the Ableton log files in the logs directory, identify error patterns, and generate a summary report. I want to break this down into manageable development tasks and then work through them step by step with proper approvals at each stage. Can you help me plan and execute this?",
      "servers": {
        "mcp-shrimp-task-manager": [
          "plan_task",
          "analyze_task",
          "split_tasks"
        ],
        "@kazuph/mcp-taskmanager": [
          "request_planning",
          "get_next_task",
          "mark_task_done",
          "approve_task_completion"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "idx": 273,
      "question": "We've been seeing recurring errors in our Ableton logs every morning around 4am. Can you help me break down the steps needed to diagnose these errors systematically? I'd like to document the investigation process while tracking the concrete actions we'll take to fix them.",
      "servers": {
